## Component Architecture

### File Structure Pattern
Each component follows this structure:

```
/src/components/[component-name]/
├── [component-name].html.twig    # Twig template
├── [component-name].scss         # Component styles
├── [component-name]-print.scss   # Print styles (optional)
├── [component-name].js           # JavaScript behavior (optional)
├── [component-name].story.js     # Storybook stories
├── [component-name].test.js      # Jest tests
├── package.json                  # Component package definition
├── README.md                     # Documentation
├── demo/
│   └── data.js                  # Demo data for stories
└── __snapshots__/               # Jest snapshots
```

### Twig Templates

**Key Conventions**:
- Parameters documented at top of file
- Internal variables prefixed with `_`
- Use `@ecl/` namespace for includes: `@ecl/icon/icon.html.twig`
- `{% apply spaceless %}` wrapper for clean HTML output
- Macros for reusable template chunks

**Example**:
```twig
{% apply spaceless %}
{# Parameters: variant, label, icon, disabled #}
{% set _css_class = 'ecl-button' %}
{% set _variant = variant|default('primary') %}

<button class="{{ _css_class }} {{ _css_class }}--{{ _variant }}">
  {% include '@ecl/icon/icon.html.twig' with {...} only %}
  <span class="{{ _css_class }}__label">{{ label }}</span>
</button>
{% endapply %}
```

### SCSS Architecture

**Modern Sass Module System**:
```scss
@use 'sass:map';
@use '@ecl/utility-screen-reader/screen-reader';
@use '@ecl/mixins-typography/mixins';

// Theme variables passed from preset
$theme: null !default;
$button: null !default;

.ecl-button {
  // BEM naming: block__element--modifier
  background: map.get($button, 'primary', 'background');
  border-radius: map.get($button, 'radius');

  &__label { /* Element */ }
  &--primary { /* Modifier */ }
  &--secondary { /* Modifier */ }
}
```

**BEM Naming**: `.ecl-[component]__[element]--[modifier]`

### JavaScript Component Pattern

```javascript
export class ComponentName {
  // Static auto-initialization
  static autoInit(root, options = {}) {
    const instance = new ComponentName(root, options);
    instance.init();
    root.ECLComponentName = instance;
    return instance;
  }

  // Supported custom events
  supportedEvents = ['onOpen', 'onClose'];

  constructor(element, options = {}) {
    this.element = element;
    this.eventManager = new EventManager();
    // Setup
  }

  init() {
    // Initialize component
    // Attach event listeners
    // Trigger 'onInit' event
  }

  // Event registration
  on(eventName, callback) {
    this.eventManager.on(eventName, callback);
  }

  // Event emission
  trigger(eventName, data) {
    this.eventManager.trigger(eventName, data);
  }

  // Cleanup
  destroy() {
    // Remove listeners
    // Clean up state
    // Trigger 'onDestroy' event
  }
}

export default ComponentName;
```

**Key Features**:
- ES6 classes with auto-init support
- EventManager for custom events
- Instance stored on DOM element
- Global `ECL.components` registry

